    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec adds an optional `birthDate` on owner create and returns a derived `ageBand` on read, computed against the owner's `registrationDate`. Since DTOs are generated from OpenAPI and read-only derived fields are computed via MapStruct expressions (matching the existing `contactPreference`/`membershipLevel`/`locality` pattern), I:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto.birthDate` and `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date` column) with getter/setter, so it survives the create\u2192GET round trip the test exercises.\n\n3. **`AgeBand.java`** (new helper, same package/style as `ContactPreference`) \u2014 computes the band from `birthDate` as of `registrationDate` (falling back to today only if unset): `<18` \u2192 `MINOR`, `18\u201364` \u2192 `ADULT`, `65+` \u2192 `SENIOR`; returns `null` when no `birthDate` so the field is simply absent.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand` mapping expression delegating to `AgeBand.of(owner)`. `birthDate` maps automatically by name into the entity.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column so JPA persistence matches the entity (tests run on `hsqldb`).\n\nThe test case (`birthDate: 1990-01-01`, registrationDate defaulting to 2026-09-07 \u2192 age 36) correctly yields `ageBand: ADULT`.",
